Add urxvt's 32 to its mouse reports

Mode 1015 sends the X10 button number, 32 included, in decimal. xterm
writes 32 for a left press and clients take the 32 off again; this wrote
0, which they read as a negative button.

--- a/src/mouse.c
+++ b/src/mouse.c
@@ -45,8 +45,10 @@
     if(!pressed)
       code = 3;
 
+    /* urxvt's numbers are X10's, 32 included, which is what a client takes
+     * off again. Without it a press read as a negative button. */
     vterm_push_output_sprintf_ctrl(state->vt, C1_CSI, "%d;%d;%dM",
-        code | modifiers, col + 1, row + 1);
+        (code | modifiers) + 0x20, col + 1, row + 1);
     break;
   }
 }
